ry\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and October to November came in under 90% of normal in 39 of those 75 years. In 2025, November to December finished at 39% of normal on the middle of the grids, after June to July came in at 65%. So far in 2026, February to March sits at 38% of normal on the middle of the grids. On grid 16659, the preliminary estimate for August to September 2026 is 40.9, a NOAA figure and not RMA&rsquo;s final index.</p>"}
